cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "When Labels Have Structure: Improving Image Classification with Hierarchy-Aware Cross-Entropy"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chan
    given-names: April
  - family-names: D'Ascenzo
    given-names: Davide
  - family-names: Cultrera di Montesano
    given-names: Sebastiano
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kidara/hierarchy-aware-cross-entropy"
url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06274"
abstract: >
  Standard cross-entropy is the default classification loss across virtually
  all of machine learning, yet it treats all misclassifications equally,
  ignoring the semantic distances that a class hierarchy encodes. We propose
  Hierarchy-Aware Cross-Entropy (HACE), a drop-in replacement for standard
  cross-entropy that incorporates a known class hierarchy directly into the
  loss via prediction aggregation and ancestral label smoothing.
keywords:
  - image classification
  - cross-entropy
  - class hierarchy
  - label smoothing
  - deep learning
